@page "/about"
<PageTitle>About these labs</PageTitle>
<h1>Choices in context</h1>
<p>These labs explore your answers to fictional situations. They do not identify a personality type, observe your real behavior, or measure ability. The profiles are reflection tools, not validated psychological assessments.</p>
<h2>Reading the evidence</h2>
<p>Repeated choices suggest a preference within the situations shown. Context comparisons use different questions, so differences may reflect wording or other circumstances. A small sample is a starting point for reflection.</p>
<p>Growth compares your choices with a suggested approach chosen by the scenario author. Agreement with that suggestion does not establish effectiveness. Changing approach is not always better, and several responses can be reasonable.</p>
<p>Connected experiments show fictional consequences based on earlier choices. They are authored possibilities, not predictions about people or the real world.</p>
<h2>Your data</h2>
<p>Answers, names, and notes remain in this browser's local storage unless you export them. There are no accounts, analytics, or external font requests. The hosting provider still receives ordinary requests for site files.</p>
<p>People on this device are separate records, not private accounts. Anyone with access to this browser can read or export them. Other applications on the same web origin can access browser storage; a separate custom domain provides stronger isolation.</p>
<p>Clearing browser data removes results. Changing the site address does not transfer them. Export a backup from <a href="saved">Saved</a> before moving or clearing data. Backup files contain every person's answers and notes; store and share them accordingly.</p>
<h2>History</h2>
<p>New results retain the questions, options, and scoring weights shown when taken. Growth runs retain their comparison baseline. Older results without question snapshots are excluded from interpretation if their test version changed; their raw answers remain available.</p>
